Seed drvd_rmp with every register that will be STORED before a call.

`VirtualRegsOpt::OptimizeVirtualRegsUsage` stores registers into the State
struct before a lifted call, and takes their values from `cur_r_inst_mp`:

    for (auto [str_er2, str_erc2] : t_bag->pres_str_rmp) {
      if (str_er2.CheckStoreBeforeCall() && !strd.contains(str_er2)) {
        ... GetRegValueFromCacheMap(str_er2, ..., cur_r_inst_mp)

`GetRegValueFromCacheMap` does `cache_map.at(t_er)`, which THROWS when the
register is absent. `cur_r_inst_mp` is seeded from `t_bag->drvd_rmp` -- every
register there gets a PHI node at the top of the block -- so the code assumes

    pres_str_rmp ∩ CheckStoreBeforeCall  ⊆  drvd_rmp

and `TraceLifter.h` documents drvd_rmp as exactly "pres_str_rmp + (pres_ld_rmp &
sucs_ld_rmp)", with no filter at all.

The seeding loop filters by `CheckPassedArgsRegs` instead, and the two
predicates are NOT the same set:

    CheckPassedArgsRegs()  -> number 0..8, or SP, for ANY reg kind
    CheckStoreBeforeCall() -> General: 0..30 or SP;  Vector: 8..15;  else SP

`CheckStoreBeforeCall` was introduced by 0007-forkemu-sync-full-gp-regs-setjmp
and is deliberately BROADER for general registers, so that glibc's hand-written
setjmp -- which snapshots x19..x28, x29, x30, sp and v8..v15 into the jmp_buf --
reads live values rather than stale globals. That patch widened the two STORE
sites and left this seeding line on the narrow predicate, so any general
register x9..x30, or vector register v8..v15, that reaches `pres_str_rmp` gets
no PHI and the `.at()` above throws:

    std::out_of_range: _Map_base::at
    #4 remill::VirtualRegsOpt::GetRegValueFromCacheMap  VroTraceLifter.cpp:1000
    #5 remill::VirtualRegsOpt::OptimizeVirtualRegsUsage VroTraceLifter.cpp:1204
    #6 remill::TraceLifter::Impl::Optimize              VroTraceLifter.cpp:135

Found on a raptormark UNIT image -- one dlopen'd library's sections emitted
alone -- which is a shape that had never been lifted before. It is not specific
to that shape: any trace whose preceding blocks store a callee-saved register
can reach it. `--norm_mode=1`, which disables this optimisation entirely, lifts
the same input to completion, which is what localised the fault to VRP.

⚠️ THE UNION, not a replacement. `CheckPassedArgsRegs` admits VECTOR registers
v0..v8 while `CheckStoreBeforeCall` admits v8..v15, so neither predicate
contains the other: swapping them would drop v0..v7 from drvd_rmp and lose PHIs
that are wanted today. Widening keeps every register the old line admitted and
adds exactly those the store loop can ask for, so the change is additive and
cannot remove a PHI that already existed.

diff --git a/backend/remill/lib/BC/VroTraceLifter.cpp b/backend/remill/lib/BC/VroTraceLifter.cpp
--- a/backend/remill/lib/BC/VroTraceLifter.cpp
+++ b/backend/remill/lib/BC/VroTraceLifter.cpp
@@ -572,8 +572,17 @@
     auto &pres_str_rmp = t_bag->pres_str_rmp;
     auto &drvd_rmp = t_bag->drvd_rmp;

     for (auto &[er1, erc1] : pres_str_rmp) {
-      if (er1.CheckPassedArgsRegs()) {
+      // The UNION of the two predicates, because neither contains the other:
+      // CheckPassedArgsRegs takes vector regs v0..v8, CheckStoreBeforeCall
+      // takes v8..v15. Dropping either side loses PHIs that are wanted.
+      //
+      // CheckStoreBeforeCall is the one that matters here: the store-before-call
+      // loop in OptimizeVirtualRegsUsage reads exactly those registers out of
+      // cur_r_inst_mp with `.at()`, and cur_r_inst_mp is seeded from drvd_rmp.
+      // Leaving them out makes that `.at()` throw std::out_of_range -- which is
+      // what 0007 did when it widened the store sites but not this line.
+      if (er1.CheckPassedArgsRegs() || er1.CheckStoreBeforeCall()) {
         drvd_rmp.insert({er1, erc1});
       }
     }
